@ 11.7 - Proto-Northeast Caucasian to Proto-Tsezic
# citation: Pogostick Man, from User:Petusek (2010), “User:Petusek/Drafts/Northeast Caucasian”. Wikipedia, the Free Encyclopedia. *b is “[p]rone to change to *m”
	{ {t͡s,st}, {t͡s:[+long]ʼ,d͡z} } > { s, t͡s }
	t͡ʃ {t͡ʃ:[+long],d͡ʒ} > ʃ t͡ʃ (the change of *t͡ʃ:[+long]ʼ is conjectured for:[+back]ezhta, as the change is only listed in P:[-voice]sez, but given the development of *t͡s:[+long]ʼ I don’t find it unreasonable to put it here)
	{ t͡ɬ, t͡ɬ:[+long]ʼ } > { ɬ, t͡ɬ }
	ɢ > q
	{ s, x:[+long] } > { z, x }
	l > l, r